WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.625 --> 00:00:30.708
After explaining the relationship

2
00:00:30.708 --> 00:00:32.541
between the jivatma,

3
00:00:32.541 --> 00:00:34.000
prakriti,

4
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.791
and Himself in the verse 14.05, Lord Krishna

5
00:00:36.791 --> 00:00:37.958
now introduces the three gunas -

6
00:00:37.958 --> 00:00:41.375
sattva, rajas, and tamas –

7
00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:44.708
which arise from material nature.

8
00:00:44.708 --> 00:00:46.000
Lord Krishna explains that

9
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.541
these three gunas bind the jivatma –

10
00:00:48.541 --> 00:00:51.750
which is truly imperishable and spiritual –

11
00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.333
to the material body.

12
00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:56.000
It is under their influence that the jivatma

13
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.125
experiences joy and sorrow.

14
00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:02.666
Although the jivatma is imperishable and divine,

15
00:01:02.666 --> 00:01:05.000
when it identifies

16
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.041
with the body

17
00:01:07.041 --> 00:01:10.041
and becomes associated with the gunas,

18
00:01:10.041 --> 00:01:14.083
it becomes caught in the cycle of birth and death.

19
00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:15.583
This verse lays the foundation

20
00:01:15.583 --> 00:01:17.458
for the detailed explanation

21
00:01:17.458 --> 00:01:20.375
of all three gunas and their effects

22
00:01:20.375 --> 00:01:21.791
in the verses that follow.

23
00:01:26.416 --> 00:01:27.666
In this verse,

24
00:01:27.666 --> 00:01:31.458
Lord Krishna explains that
sattva, rajas, and tamas –

25
00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:32.333
these three gunas

26
00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:34.958
arise from material prakriti

27
00:01:34.958 --> 00:01:35.958
and influence

28
00:01:35.958 --> 00:01:38.833
every behaviour in the world.

29
00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:41.833
The jivatma is truly avyaya –

30
00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:46.166
imperishable, unchanging, and transcendental.

31
00:01:46.166 --> 00:01:49.875
But when it comes into contact with prakriti,

32
00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:54.000
it becomes bound under the influence
of these gunas.

33
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000
Nibadhnanti means ‘to bind.’

34
00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.250
These gunas bind the soul

35
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:00.208
to the material

36
00:02:00.208 --> 00:02:02.666
body like invisible ropes,

37
00:02:02.666 --> 00:02:07.666
compelling it to act according to whichever

38
00:02:07.666 --> 00:02:10.375
guna is dominant at that moment.

39
00:02:10.375 --> 00:02:13.083
Lord Krishna addresses Arjun as Mahabaho –

40
00:02:13.083 --> 00:02:14.625
reminding him

41
00:02:14.625 --> 00:02:17.416
that even a powerful warrior

42
00:02:17.416 --> 00:02:19.916
cannot remain untouched by these gunas

43
00:02:19.916 --> 00:02:21.125
as long as he is

44
00:02:21.125 --> 00:02:24.000
in the body.

45
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.375
This means that

46
00:02:25.375 --> 00:02:27.166
no person –

47
00:02:27.166 --> 00:02:29.291
however powerful,

48
00:02:29.291 --> 00:02:32.375
learned, or highly placed –

49
00:02:32.375 --> 00:02:35.000
cannot  escape the hold of these gunas

50
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.166
until they rise above them.

51
00:02:38.166 --> 00:02:40.291
These gunas are not merely ideas –

52
00:02:40.291 --> 00:02:43.666
they are subtle forces that govern

53
00:02:43.666 --> 00:02:45.500
the relationship between consciousness

54
00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.416
and matter.

55
00:02:47.416 --> 00:02:52.500
They shape our vision, thoughts, and reactions.

56
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.208
For example – a person under the
influence of sattva

57
00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:57.083
responds with peace

58
00:02:57.083 --> 00:03:00.500
and thoughtfulness.

59
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.333
A person under rajas

60
00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:05.625
acts with haste and excitement.

61
00:03:05.625 --> 00:03:09.000
A person under tamas stops,

62
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.750
becomes indecisive,

63
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:14.000
or acts inappropriately.

64
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.625
These gunas continuously influence

65
00:03:16.625 --> 00:03:17.833
our thoughts,

66
00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:18.666
emotions,

67
00:03:18.666 --> 00:03:21.083
and actions like invisible threads,

68
00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:23.333
and this is what determines the jivatma’s

69
00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:25.208
worldly experience.

70
00:03:25.208 --> 00:03:28.375
Although the soul is beyond them,
its attachment

71
00:03:28.375 --> 00:03:30.125
to the body and its desires

72
00:03:30.125 --> 00:03:32.416
binds it.

73
00:03:32.416 --> 00:03:35.708
Lord Krishna will now explain in
detail the characteristics

74
00:03:35.708 --> 00:03:38.875
and effects of all three gunas,

75
00:03:38.875 --> 00:03:42.833
so that Arjun – and we – can understand

76
00:03:42.833 --> 00:03:46.000
how they shape our lives

77
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.541
and how we can rise above them.

78
00:03:54.166 --> 00:03:56.166
You say –

79
00:03:56.166 --> 00:03:59.125
‘I am free!’

80
00:03:59.125 --> 00:04:02.291
But are you truly?

81
00:04:02.291 --> 00:04:05.958
When you say ‘I am just like this’

82
00:04:05.958 --> 00:04:09.541
or ‘I need this’ –

83
00:04:09.541 --> 00:04:13.458
often this does not come from your true nature.

84
00:04:13.458 --> 00:04:15.958
It comes from the grip of the three gunas –

85
00:04:15.958 --> 00:04:18.458
sattva, rajas,

86
00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:19.500
and tamas.

87
00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:24.166
You are neither the mind,

88
00:04:24.166 --> 00:04:29.166
nor the voice that keeps speaking within.

89
00:04:29.166 --> 00:04:32.291
That voice too has been shaped over time –

90
00:04:32.291 --> 00:04:33.750
by your company,

91
00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:37.291
your experiences, your environment.

92
00:04:37.291 --> 00:04:39.208
For example –

93
00:04:39.208 --> 00:04:43.500
you already have a vehicle that
meets your needs.

94
00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.791
But when a friend or neighbour

95
00:04:45.791 --> 00:04:48.583
buys a newer model,

96
00:04:48.583 --> 00:04:49.458
if your mind too

97
00:04:49.458 --> 00:04:53.458
begins to crave one,

98
00:04:53.458 --> 00:04:55.208
pause and reflect –

99
00:04:55.208 --> 00:04:57.666
this is not a genuine need.

100
00:04:57.666 --> 00:05:00.666
It is a petty competitive impulse

101
00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:05.458
born from the influence of these three gunas.

102
00:05:05.458 --> 00:05:06.625
Not getting entangled

103
00:05:06.625 --> 00:05:09.708
in their bondage is liberation itself.

104
00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:13.083
I watch from within as the witness.

105
00:05:13.083 --> 00:05:14.250
I see

106
00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.291
how these gunas bind you –

107
00:05:17.291 --> 00:05:20.416
how they make you believe that

108
00:05:20.416 --> 00:05:22.041
your momentary feelings

109
00:05:22.041 --> 00:05:26.541
and reactions are your identity.

110
00:05:26.541 --> 00:05:28.833
But this is not the truth.

111
00:05:28.833 --> 00:05:31.416
You are beyond them.

112
00:05:31.416 --> 00:05:33.083
You are eternal.

113
00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:35.875
The moment you begin to recognise

114
00:05:35.875 --> 00:05:40.000
how these gunas operate, that very moment

115
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.666
a new freedom is experienced –

116
00:05:43.666 --> 00:05:45.833
not the freedom to react,

117
00:05:45.833 --> 00:05:48.000
but the freedom to respond.

118
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.750
Grow this awareness.

119
00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:54.708
I will free you from these bondages

120
00:05:54.708 --> 00:05:58.083
and lead you to your true nature.

121
00:06:02.833 --> 00:06:05.083
Have you ever wondered –

122
00:06:05.083 --> 00:06:08.708
why do two people living in the same family

123
00:06:08.708 --> 00:06:13.666
see the same situation in
completely different ways?

124
00:06:13.666 --> 00:06:16.416
One sees an opportunity,

125
00:06:16.416 --> 00:06:18.250
the other sees a threat.

126
00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.916
One wants to talk,

127
00:06:19.916 --> 00:06:22.000
the other goes quiet.

128
00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.000
And even when you try lovingly to explain,

129
00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.833
the other person simply does not understand.

130
00:06:28.833 --> 00:06:33.791
The reason is subtle – but profound.

131
00:06:33.791 --> 00:06:35.416
All of our behaviour,

132
00:06:35.416 --> 00:06:37.625
thinking, and reactions

133
00:06:37.625 --> 00:06:41.166
depend on which guna is dominant within us

134
00:06:41.166 --> 00:06:44.041
at that moment –

135
00:06:44.041 --> 00:06:47.458
sattva, rajas, or tamas.

136
00:06:47.458 --> 00:06:50.208
This is not merely a difference in personality.

137
00:06:50.208 --> 00:06:52.416
It is a difference in the inner lens

138
00:06:52.416 --> 00:06:55.791
through which we are seeing the world.

139
00:06:55.791 --> 00:06:57.708
And most of the time,

140
00:06:57.708 --> 00:06:59.083
we do not even realise

141
00:06:59.083 --> 00:07:01.875
that this lens is binding us.

142
00:07:01.875 --> 00:07:03.500
This is why family conflicts

143
00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.625
often seem to arise from nowhere.

144
00:07:06.625 --> 00:07:08.458
We are not actually clashing over facts –

145
00:07:08.458 --> 00:07:11.208
we are clashing through the lens

146
00:07:11.208 --> 00:07:13.958
of our own inner gunas.

147
00:07:13.958 --> 00:07:16.416
So when someone’s reaction

148
00:07:16.416 --> 00:07:21.208
disturbs you, pause and think –

149
00:07:21.208 --> 00:07:24.208
is this their true nature,

150
00:07:24.208 --> 00:07:28.291
or is it the shadow of the guna active
within them at this moment?

151
00:07:28.291 --> 00:07:30.375
This does not mean ignoring

152
00:07:30.375 --> 00:07:32.958
wrong behaviour.

153
00:07:32.958 --> 00:07:37.416
But this understanding will help you

154
00:07:37.416 --> 00:07:39.208
respond with empathy

155
00:07:39.208 --> 00:07:40.958
rather than a harsh judgement.

156
00:07:40.958 --> 00:07:44.541
This understanding softens relationships.

157
00:07:44.541 --> 00:07:47.833
It creates space in the mind.

158
00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:49.166
And perhaps

159
00:07:49.166 --> 00:07:52.291
this is the bridge where family begins to value

160
00:07:52.291 --> 00:07:55.416
‘understanding’ more than ‘being right.’

161
00:07:55.416 --> 00:07:59.791
Instead of immediately accepting
every thought that arises,

162
00:07:59.791 --> 00:08:02.708
pause, reflect, and then decide.

163
00:08:02.708 --> 00:08:04.958
These decisions will be real –

164
00:08:04.958 --> 00:08:08.625
and will not entangle you in the gunas’ bondage,

165
00:08:08.625 --> 00:08:10.583
rather it will free you.

166
00:08:15.375 --> 00:08:18.375
You think you are free –

167
00:08:18.375 --> 00:08:23.416
to think, to decide, to act.

168
00:08:23.416 --> 00:08:26.208
But step back and look –

169
00:08:26.208 --> 00:08:29.666
are your thoughts truly your own,

170
00:08:29.666 --> 00:08:31.583
or are they a product of the environment

171
00:08:31.583 --> 00:08:33.666
where you work?

172
00:08:33.666 --> 00:08:36.666
When a new member joins your team,

173
00:08:36.666 --> 00:08:40.416
they do not arrive with fixed habits.

174
00:08:40.416 --> 00:08:42.458
But within a short time,

175
00:08:42.458 --> 00:08:44.541
they begin to absorb the pace,

176
00:08:44.541 --> 00:08:48.125
tone, and energy of your workplace.

177
00:08:48.125 --> 00:08:50.125
Just as the soul,

178
00:08:50.125 --> 00:08:53.125
coming into contact with material energy,

179
00:08:53.125 --> 00:08:55.166
becomes influenced by the gunas –

180
00:08:55.166 --> 00:08:59.041
As a leader, you may not even realise

181
00:08:59.041 --> 00:09:00.833
that your reactions,

182
00:09:00.833 --> 00:09:01.916
your mood,

183
00:09:01.916 --> 00:09:05.166
and your way of handling stress

184
00:09:05.166 --> 00:09:06.833
gradually become

185
00:09:06.833 --> 00:09:10.375
the cultural identity that others absorb.

186
00:09:10.375 --> 00:09:13.791
You are not only doing your work –

187
00:09:13.791 --> 00:09:17.625
you are also spreading an invisible influence.

188
00:09:17.625 --> 00:09:21.416
Even as an employee, embracing the thinking

189
00:09:21.416 --> 00:09:23.750
of management and seniors

190
00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:27.875
builds your image as a committed professional

191
00:09:27.875 --> 00:09:31.500
and helps both you and your colleagues

192
00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.750
become more productive.

193
00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:37.375
Culture spreads not only through rules,

194
00:09:37.375 --> 00:09:39.916
but through energy.

195
00:09:39.916 --> 00:09:42.125
So the question is –

196
00:09:42.125 --> 00:09:47.708
which guna are you spreading in
your workplace:

197
00:09:47.708 --> 00:09:51.958
sattva, rajas, or tamas?

198
00:09:51.958 --> 00:09:55.666
You cannot escape influence.

199
00:09:55.666 --> 00:09:58.583
But with awareness,

200
00:09:58.583 --> 00:10:04.208
you can choose what you pass forward.
